---
<Base title={"Buying a Hotel from a Receiver"} description={"How we bid on hotels in receivership: as the stalking horse under court-approved bid procedures, with a deposit, as-is, and a purchase agreement written for a sale order."}>
  <Hero eyebrow={"For receivers and counsel"} title={"Buying a hotel from a receiver."} lead={"We bid in a form a court can approve. The sale is the court's to approve, and the hotel has to keep operating until the day it transfers."} />
  <SectionNav section="receivers" />
  <main id="main">
<section class="section"><div class="wrap intro">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">How we bid</p><h2>A buyer who understands what a receiver has to deliver.</h2>
        <div class="body"><p>A receiver needs a buyer who understands that the sale is the court's to approve, that the property is sold as it stands, and that the hotel has to keep operating until the day it transfers.</p></div></div>
      <dl class="pillars">
        <div><dt>Subject to court approval</dt><dd>Our purchase agreements are written for a <a href="/glossary/#sale-order">sale order</a>, with the receiver's customary limits on representations.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Opening bidder</dt><dd>We will serve as the initial bidder, the <a href="/glossary/#stalking-horse">stalking horse</a>, under court-approved overbid procedures.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Deposit on signing</dt><dd>We post a deposit when the agreement is signed.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>As-is</dt><dd>We complete our diligence before we sign and take the hotel in its present condition, <a href="/glossary/#as-is">as-is, where-is</a>.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">How a receiver's sale usually runs</p><h2>From the order of appointment to the sale order.</h2>
        <p>Procedures differ by court and by state. This is a general outline, so that counsel can see where a bid fits.</p></div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><h3>Appointment</h3><p>The court appoints a receiver. The order of appointment sets the receiver's authority: to operate the hotel, retain a manager, and control the accounts.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Stabilize and market</h3><p>The receiver keeps the hotel operating and reports to the court. With the court's approval, the receiver markets the property.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Stalking horse agreement</h3><p>A buyer signs a purchase agreement, subject to court approval. Its price and terms are the opening bid.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Bid procedures and overbid</h3><p>The receiver asks the court to approve <a href="/glossary/#bid-procedures">bid procedures</a> that let other buyers submit higher bids. If more than one qualified bid comes in, there is an auction.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Sale hearing</h3><p>The court hears the motion to approve the sale and, if satisfied, enters the sale order.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Closing</h3><p>The sale closes under the order. Taxes and other balances are settled as the order provides, and the hotel transfers.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Beyond the bid</p><h2>What a receiver can count on after the agreement is signed.</h2></div>
      <div class="cells">
        <div><h3>Proof of funds</h3><p>Provided with a bid. We do not rely on third-party financing to close a purchase.</p></div>
        <div><h3>A hotel that stays open</h3><p>The franchise, the management company, the liquor license, bookings, staff, and taxes all have to carry over. <a class="more arrow" href="/receivers/keeping-the-hotel-open/">How we handle the transition</a></p></div>
        <div><h3>A principal on the other end</h3><p>We respond to receivers and counsel directly. <a class="more arrow" href="/receivers/what-we-ask-for/">What we ask for</a></p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

        <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Related reading</p></div><ul class="toc"><li><a href="/library/receivership/">Keeping a hotel open through receivership <span>Library</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#receivership">Receiver and receivership <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#stalking-horse">Stalking horse bidder <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/blog/foreclosure-timelines-and-hotel-value/">Foreclosure timelines and why they matter more for hotels <span>Blog</span></a></li></ul></div></section>
  </main>
  <Cta title={"Tell us about the hotel and the case."} text={"We respond to receivers and counsel directly."} label={"Discuss a receivership"} />
</Base>
